<article class="env-definition" id="0EPU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EPU">Definition <span data-tag="0EPU">72.7.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be a locally Noetherian integral algebraic space over $S$. Let $\mathcal{L}$ be an invertible $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
For any nonzero meromorphic section $s$ of $\mathcal{L}$ we define the <em>Weil divisor associated to $s$</em> as 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \text{div}_\mathcal {L}(s) = \sum \text{ord}_{Z, \mathcal{L}}(s) [Z] \in \text{Div}(X)  \]
</div>
<p>
 where the sum is over prime divisors. This is well defined by Lemma <a href="/tag/0EPS" data-tag="0EPS">72.7.2</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We define <em>Weil divisor class associated to $\mathcal{L}$</em> as the image of $\text{div}_\mathcal {L}(s)$ in $\text{Cl}(X)$ where $s$ is any nonzero meromorphic section of $\mathcal{L}$ over $X$. This is well defined by Lemma <a href="/tag/0EPT" data-tag="0EPT">72.7.3</a>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>